I run Yaad-e-Namaz, a free prayer times site with no ads. The page people use the most by far is the Qibla finder, which shows Muslims the direction of the Kaaba in Makkah. I wanted it to work straight in the phone browser, without asking anyone to install an app. Here's how it works and what tripped me up.
The Qibla isn't "the direction on a flat map". It's the start of the shortest path over the globe to the Kaaba (21.4225° N, 39.8262° E). That's a standard initial bearing calculation:
